Tether Node Debian package
==========================

This package installs a system service named tether-node.service. The service
runs as root so the managed Node can use the approved system package updater
and perform its configured device-management operations. Install or upgrade
the package with APT as root so its declared LibreOffice runtime dependencies
are installed from the configured Debian repositories:

    sudo apt install ./Tether-node-runtime-@TETHER_VERSION@-linux-x64.deb

The service does not receive broad sudo rules because it already runs under
systemd as root.

The Node service manages EasyTier networks with the dedicated no-login
`tether-easytier` system account. Its private network configuration is stored
under `/var/lib/tether-easytier`; the EasyTier core runs through `setpriv`
without TUN or elevated capabilities. The `tether-node` service itself remains
the system-level manager and update owner.

On first installation the service remains stopped until the Node is paired.
Create a one-time pairing code in the Tether APP, then run this command from a
terminal:

    sudo tether-node-pair

It asks for the Hub WebSocket URL if one is not configured, then prompts for
the one-time code without echoing it. The Node uses its hostname as the device
id unless TETHER_DEVICE is already configured. On success it writes the
credential to the root-private /etc/tether-node/node.env file and enables the
service. Node identity, database, logs, and private runtime state stay outside
the package under /var/lib/tether-node.

If pairing completed but the service did not start, run:

    systemctl enable --now tether-node.service

The signed preview channel is selected for this candidate package. The package
manager owns Debian runtime updates; the legacy per-file Node updater is not
used. Removing the package keeps /var/lib/tether-node data and credentials.
